# CORE_UX — documentation (mandatory)

The HTML reference in **`doc/`** is part of the kit contract. **Do not ship component, token, or catalog changes without updating the doc in the same change set.**

Canonical detail: `ai-instructions/components.md` (section « Documentation maintenance »).

## Same change set — always update

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New `<core-*>` tag | `doc/components/core-<name>.html` + `doc/assets/sidebar.js` + `doc/index.html` card grid + `COMPONENTS.md` |
| Removed tag | Delete page + sidebar entry + index card + `COMPONENTS.md` row |
| New/changed attribute | Attribute table + live demo on component page |
| New/changed event or public method | Events/API section + demo when applicable |
| Composable sub-tag (menu-item, tab, notif-host, …) | Parent page documents **each tag** in the group (no separate sidebar entry required) |
| New/changed design token | `styles/tokens.css`, `tailwind.preset.js`, `THEMING.md`, `doc/theming.html`, affected component pages |
| Shared form-control attrs | `doc/form-controls.html` when scope changes |

Also sync:

- **`doc/index.html`** — hero tag/page counts and `card-grid` entries
- **`doc/assets/sidebar.js`** — nav links and brand count (`25 pages · 30 tags` or current totals)
- **`COMPONENTS.md`** — short index aligned with `index.js`

## Doc page checklist

- Attributes = `observedAttributes` + slot patterns (`data-core-footer`) + attrs read at connect (note if not reactive)
- Events = outward `CustomEvent` names and `detail` shape
- Methods = public imperative API (`openMenu`, `show`, `deselectVisible`, …)
- Live demos for every documented variant/state
- Valid HTML (no corrupted doctype or broken import maps)

## Do not

- Merge component/CSS/token changes without touching `doc/` when the public API or catalog changed
- Add sidebar entries for composable sub-tags when the parent page already documents them
- Rely on silent attribute fallbacks — document supported values explicitly
